module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.ProperCohomologyFiniteness
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.Setup
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# Finiteness of the cohomology of a coherent module on `Proj A`

Let `A` be a graded ring with `A₀` Noetherian, generated by finitely many elements of `A₁` over
`A₀`, and let `X = Proj A`. This file proves assertion (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0AG6]: for every
coherent `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ` and every `p` the cohomology `H^p(X, ℱ)` is a finite `A₀`-module.

The generation hypothesis makes `A` a finitely generated `A₀`-algebra, so the structure morphism
`X ⟶ Spec A₀` is proper; `A₀` is Noetherian; and [Stacks, Tag 02O6] over the base ring is proved
unconditionally as `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.tag02O6`. That is the whole
proof. The source reaches the assertion through a closed immersion into `ℙⁿ_{A₀}` and clause (3)
of [Stacks, Tag 01YS]; the proper-mapping theorem is available in this library and subsumes that
route, so the closed immersion is used only where it is unavoidable — in
`../ProjCoherentDegreeOne/DegreeSections.lean`, for Serre's computation of the sections of the
twisting sheaves.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne.moduleFinite_cohomology_of_isCoherent`: **assertion (2) of
  [Stacks, Tag 0AG6]**.

## Implementation notes

The `A₀`-module structure is restriction of scalars along the canonical structure morphism
`AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.toSpecZero`, which is what
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.specAlgebraRingHom` unfolds to; the cohomology
is `Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.cohomologyOf`, the right derived functor of
module-valued global sections. Both are written out here so that the statement reads without the
intermediate vocabulary.

No `stacks` attribute is attached in this file; the tag is registered on the conjunction of all
its assertions in `../ProjCoherentDegreeOne/Main.lean`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG6)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 02O6](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/02O6)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory
open AlgebraicGeometry.ProjectiveSpectrum.Proj
open Stacks.Cohomology.AffineBase (moduleGlobalSections)

universe u w

namespace Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne

attribute [local instance] HasDerivedCategory.standard

variable {A : Type u} {σ : Type w} [CommRing A] [SetLike σ A] [AddSubgroupClass σ A]
  (𝒜 : ℕ → σ) [GradedRing 𝒜] [IsNoetherianRing (𝒜 0)] {n : ℕ} (x : Fin (n + 1) → A)
  (hgen : Algebra.adjoin (𝒜 0) (Set.range x) = ⊤)

include hgen

/-- **Assertion (2) of [Stacks, Tag 0AG6].** For every coherent `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ` on
`X = Proj A` and every `p`, the cohomology `H^p(X, ℱ)` is a finite `A₀`-module.

`X` is proper over `Spec A₀` because `A` is a finitely generated `A₀`-algebra, and `A₀` is
Noetherian, so this is [Stacks, Tag 02O6] over the base ring. -/
@[ega "III 2.2.2"]
theorem moduleFinite_cohomology_of_isCoherent
    (F : (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜).Modules) (hF : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent F) (q : ℕ) :
    Module.Finite (𝒜 0)
      ((ModuleCat.restrictScalars ((Scheme.ΓSpecIso (.of (𝒜 0))).inv ≫
          (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.toSpecZero 𝒜).appTop).hom).obj
        (((moduleGlobalSections (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜)).rightDerived q).obj F)) :=
  have := finiteType 𝒜 x hgen
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GradedProperCohomology.tag02O6 (𝒜 0) inferInstance
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj 𝒜) (AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.toSpecZero 𝒜) inferInstance F hF q

end Stacks.ProjCoherentDegreeOne

end
